    "description": "Parker\nLucite and Metal Fountain Pen\nMid-Century Modern, Circa 1940s-1950s\nThis vintage Parker \"51\" fountain pen features the model's signature streamlined silhouette, introduced originally in 1941 to revolutionize writing instruments. The design highlights a tapered black barrel, an integrated hooded nib assembly, and a brushed metal lustraloy-style slip-on cap with an arrow clip. It comes housed in its vintage clamshell presentation box lined with satin and fitted card stock.\nParker \"51\" aerodynamic design with hooded nib and streamlined profile\nBlack resin/lucite barrel with brushed metal cap and silver-tone arrow pocket clip\nMarked \"51\" and \"Parker\" on inner presentation case insert\nIncludes hinged presentation box measuring approximately 5.6 inches in length\nCondition:\nVintage condition with age-appropriate cosmetic wear. Barrel and hood show light surface micro-scratching consistent with handling and use. Cap retains its clip firmly and seats securely. Box exterior exhibits scuffs, edge wear, and surface rubbing; interior card shows vintage handwriting in ink across the lower bezel. Untested for ink filling and writing functionality.",
